{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/874129-documentaries-for-dark-eras","id":874129,"title":"Documentaries for Dark Eras?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-25T17:41:41-07:00","id":874129,"title":"Documentaries for Dark Eras?","content":"Anyone have any good documentaries on streaming services for historical reference to various Dark Eras? I'm specifically looking for a good neolithic one, but I figure it'd be cool to compile a list.<br /> <br /> On Netflix I found these two<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://https://www.netflix.com/title/80036400\" target=\"_blank\">The Sixties</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.netflix.com/title/80030186\" target=\"_blank\">The Seventies</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T19:19:13-07:00","id":874182,"title":"","content":"Not film--I'm not the hugest fan of documentaries--but I recommend the books <i>Rape and Sexual Power in Early America</i> by Sharon Block, and <i>White Women and Black Men: Illicit Sex in the 19th Century South</i> by Martha Hodes for a Dark Era coming in the Companion. I can't help with Neolithic, but are you looking for academic sources for any other Era? If you give me some specific ones, I'm sure I have other books to recommend, and I can ask my cohort as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T19:44:48-07:00","id":874205,"title":"","content":"(Also, related, since I don't want you to think I'm just avoiding your question.<br /> <br /> My undergraduate adviser for whom I also TAd a class on the Vikings was Mary Frances Giandrea. You can look her up. She was grad student to Robin Fleming at Boston College. Anyway, Professor Giandrea used to always rant to me in both Viking World and the class on the Crusades that I took with her on how shitty documentaries for her Fields of Interest and before were. She hated that she didn't have anything good to show her students who learned best from video. Obviously, the Neolithic is much earlier to this as well, but my point is, according to my undergraduate adviser, there's not much documentary content that's all that great for anything before, like, the 1600s, though she's also not much of a documentary fan in general.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:24:06-07:00","id":874226,"title":"","content":"Yeah obviously documentaries especially on prehistorical subjects are going to result in a lot of conjecture and theory. I mostly like them because I can turn them on and do other things concurrently.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/news/uk-21806135\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.bbc.com/news/uk-21806135</a> This is interesting on Neolithic Housing, not the Vinca region but still...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:32:04-07:00","id":874230,"title":"","content":"My own Fields of Interest are much, much later, even from what my undergrad adviser did, so I can't help with Neolithic anything. I'm sorry =(.<br /> <br /> I hope some others come who can help with that, but if anyone has questions for me about book or journal sources, please ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:34:05-07:00","id":874231,"title":"","content":"As far as interest in other periods, of course. I think the next story I run will probably be Neolithic, though I've considered, Alexander, Vikings, Fall of Constantinople, Cold War and Gang/Drug War (Bowery Dogs, haven't actually read it). Hard to choose, though in some ways I think I prefer this pre-internet eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 04-25-2016, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:43:53-07:00","id":874236,"title":"","content":"I took an intellectual history course on the Cold War where the first half of the week was a lecture situating us in a different decade of the Cold War, and then we read a spy novel set in that decade. I would recommend doing something in that kind of structure prior to a Cold War game, given how much of the period revolved around propaganda and the dissemination of information and who thought what and why. Also, perhaps Samantha Smith could be involved in some capacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T21:27:26-07:00","id":874249,"title":"","content":"Not documentaries per say, but there are a lot of great historical podcasts out there that cover the eras well. The most notable are probably <a href=\"http://www.dancarlin.com/hardcore-history-series/\" target=\"_blank\">Hardcore History</a> and <a href=\"http://thehistoryofrome.typepad.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The History of Rome/Revolutions</a>, the latter of which are actually two separate podcasts by the same person.<br /> <br /> Hardcore History has touched on Alexander multiple times (&quot;Alexander vs Hitler&quot;, &quot;History Under the Influence&quot;) and is about to again once they get past Xerxes in their &quot;Kings of Kings.&quot; &quot;Macedonian Soap Opera is specifically about the line &quot;to the strongest.&quot; Dan also has a really neat episode called Thor's Angels that is more focused on the relationship of the Goths to Christianity, but as the title implies, there's lots about the Norse as well. &quot;Ghosts of the Ostfront&quot; may not be Cold War Berlin, but it does definitely colour the feelings of the Soviets and Germans following WWII.<br /> <br /> History of Rome is obvious, but it really is the best and will be invaluable once we get Cleopatrian Mummy and Forsaken by Rome. Otherwise, it's great for Requiem for Rome.<br /> <br /> Revolutions has covered the English Revolution, the American Revolution, the French Revolution/Napoleonic Wars, and the Haitian Revolution. I'm actually way behind listening to this one, so I don't know if more revolutions are upcoming. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/TheGreatWar\" target=\"_blank\">The Great War</a> on YouTube also goes through WWI with a week-by-week account, 100 years later (so it won't be done for another two and half years).<br /> <br /> If you are willing to spend some dough, <a href=\"http://www.thegreatcourses.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Great Courses</a> has tonnes of content on pretty much all eras. Just wait until they are on sale, or you will go bankrupt. They do have a good course on <a href=\"http://www.thegreatcourses.com/courses/human-prehistory-and-the-first-civilizations.html\" target=\"_blank\">Human Prehistory</a> that will cover the Neolithic era although I haven't watched those episodes, so I can't say of the Vinca are mentioned. Unfortunately, it is not on their <a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/\" target=\"_blank\">streaming service</a>, so you've have to pay for the individual course, but it is on sale right now. If that changes, wait a month, then it should be on sale again.<br /> <br /> While it's not a documentary, I'd strongly suggest that anyone interested in running a chronicle in Europe anywhere from 1840-1920 watch the BBC miniseries Fall of Eagles. It's not 100% accurate, but it is a very good presentation of the German, Austrian, Russian, and English royal families in the aftermath of the Napoleonic Wars and the run up to WWI. Very watchable, and contains the sublime casting of young Patrick Stewart as Vladimir freaking Lenin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 04-26-2016, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T21:54:03-07:00","id":874261,"title":"","content":"Found this one on <a href=\"http://www.hulu.com/watch/437711\" target=\"_blank\">stone henge </a> which will explain how the god machine convinced man to build arcane stone occult matrices with golden wizard hats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 04-26-2016, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T00:02:43-07:00","id":874313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/874129-documentaries-for-dark-eras?p=874182#post874182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not film--I'm not the hugest fan of documentaries--but I recommend the books <i>Rape and Sexual Power in Early America</i> by Sharon Block, and <i>White Women and Black Men: Illicit Sex in the 19th Century South</i> by Martha Hodes for a Dark Era coming in the Companion. I can't help with Neolithic, but are you looking for academic sources for any other Era? If you give me some specific ones, I'm sure I have other books to recommend, and I can ask my cohort as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit of an awkward position here, since the single most influential &quot;history film&quot; ever was about this era... and its cultural impact can't be overlooked... but it's one of the most truly evil cultural watershed moments in US history, and is based on unmitigated lies, so I hesitate to &quot;recommend&quot; it.<br /> <br /> I suppose it would be relevant for studying up on a 19-teens and 20s era (the era it was made and culturally impacted) and not the Reconstruction era (the era it lies about).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T05:57:03-07:00","id":874455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/874129-documentaries-for-dark-eras?p=874313#post874313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a bit of an awkward position here, since the single most influential &quot;history film&quot; ever was about this era... and its cultural impact can't be overlooked... but it's one of the most truly evil cultural watershed moments in US history, and is based on unmitigated lies, so I hesitate to &quot;recommend&quot; it.<br /> <br /> I suppose it would be relevant for studying up on a 19-teens and 20s era (the era it was made and culturally impacted) and not the Reconstruction era (the era it lies about).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But as I said, I'm not a documentary fan, and I'm definitely not going to drop THAT title. I didn't say &quot;there are no good documentaries ever&quot;, I said that I didn't like documentaries and had none to recommend. I mean, I just woke up, so maybe that's it, but what's an awkward position about that =P?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T06:02:10-07:00","id":874460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/874129-documentaries-for-dark-eras?p=874249#post874249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/TheGreatWar\" target=\"_blank\">The Great War</a> on YouTube also goes through WWI with a week-by-week account, 100 years later (so it won't be done for another two and half years).</div> </div> </div> </div>Off to watch this now. And if anyone is interested in book recs on WWI, I took a seminar on WWI and have a whole lot of good books I can recommend, so that you don't end up reading Chris Clark or Niall Ferguson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"ht